  "implementationDetails": {
    "audioStrategy": "One AudioContext. Piano Grand, Upright, and Electric play bundled recorded MP3 sample sets (nearest root, two velocity layers, playbackRate for the sounding pitch). Clav, Digital, and Misc are live synthesis. If the recorded library is absent, Grand keeps the Phase 1 additive voice and Upright/Electric use distinct synthesis. If a recorded set fails to load, those three types play a labeled synthesized fallback and the status is fallback, not ready. Each piano layer has its own bus and effect chain. Organ (two layers, one chain) and Synth A/B/C are live synthesis on extra buses into the same master and the same rotary. Layer level is applied before the direct/rotary split so layers stay independent into the shared rotary. Master gain and one limiter feed a single destination. Programs round-trip the document; Master Level and live pedal/wheel positions are not stored.",
